<title>UK: Hemingway in Sainsbury lease deal.</title>
<headline>Hemingway in Sainsbury lease deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>British property group Hemingway Properties Plc said on Monday it signed a new lease deal with supermarket chain J Sainsbury Plc.</p>
<p>Under the terms of the deal for the supermarket centre in Oxford, Hemingway said it agreed to pay Sainsbury 3.5 million stg.</p>
<p>In return, Sainsbury would replace its existing leases, which had a rental income of 7,000 stg per annum, with a new 25-year lease which would produce an increase in initial annual income to Hemingway of 467,000 stg.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
